Summary
──────────────────────────────
• Instead of holding a reference to transform (via startMarker), store the starting position in a Vector3.
• Update the interpolation (Lerp) using the stored start position and your computed endPos.
• Reorder your calculation of distance and journeyAmount so that you first compute the elapsed distance, then update the ratio.
• Consider using a flag or storing the Coroutine handle if you need more control over stopping the coroutine.

With these adjustments, endPos will remain fixed, and your card’s movement should interpolate as expected.

